// Title: PSEXEC Remote Execution File Artefact
// Sigma ID: 304afd73-55a5-4bb9-8c21-0b1fc84ea9e4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-21 | Modified: 2023-02-23
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1136.002, T1543.003, T1570, S0029
// Description: Detects creation of the PSEXEC key file. Which is created anytime a PsExec command is executed.
//   It gets written to the file system and will be recorded in the USN Journal on the target system
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://aboutdfir.com/the-key-to-identify-psexec/
//   - https://twitter.com/davisrichardg/status/1616518800584704028
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_sysinternals_psexec_service_key.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\PSEXEC-" and FolderPath endswith ".key"
